# Regression pin for the `'atomic` binding-permission fix (see CHANGELOG.md's
# [Unreleased] entry and docs/qualifiers.md's `'atomic` "Binding permission"
# section): `'atomic` now requires `mut`/`var mut` for every mutating op
# (compound assign, plain store, `.swap()`), enforced in
# `src/checker/mod.rs`'s `check_assign_target` and
# `src/transpiler/emit_methods.rs`'s `try_emit_atomic_method`.
#
# That new rule must NOT retroactively apply to a name promoted from `'actor`/
# `'guard` to the `'atomic` representation by the automatic promotion pass
# (`src/transpiler/promote_atomic.rs`, docs/qualifiers.md's "Automatic
# 'actor/'guard -> 'atomic promotion" section) — promotion is purely additive
# and behavior-preserving, and must carry forward whatever permission the
# pre-promotion `'actor`/`'guard` declaration already had, not the new,
# stricter `'atomic`-specific rule. `counter` below is declared with a bare
# `var` (no `mut`) — already legal for a scalar `'actor` under the pre-existing
# generic rebind-permission rule — and every promotion criterion holds (atomic-
# eligible scalar, never escapes the function, every access is a single
# recognized primitive, never used inside a `with` block), so this must both
# compile AND run to the documented result, exercising the promotion pass
# end-to-end with BOTH a compound-assign and a `.swap()` on the same name.
#
# See tests/atomic_qualifier.rs's
# `promotion_still_permits_mutation_on_a_bare_var_actor_source_after_binding_permission_fix`
# for the matching codegen-inspection half (confirms the atomic representation
# — Arc<AtomicIsize>/fetch_add/fetch_sub/swap — is really what gets emitted,
# not just that this fixture's stdout happens to match).
def main():
    var counter'actor = 0
    counter += 5
    counter -= 2
    let old = counter.swap(100)
    print "{counter} {old}"
